Ladybird now aligns a box under middle, sub, or super against the
metrics of its parent box: the parent’s x-height for middle, and its
font size for sub and super. Blink takes them from the parent box too,
in InlineLayoutStateStack::ApplyBaselineShift(), and so does WebKit,
in LineBoxVerticalAligner::logicalTopOffsetFromParentBaseline(). Gecko’s
nsLineLayout::VerticalAlignFrames() takes the font metrics of the
parent span. Blink and WebKit add 1px to the sub and super shifts, which
Ladybird and Gecko don’t, so those two cases come out 1px apart.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5 ran
the six cases of the test added here. They agree on the middle cases,
which Ladybird now matches. For sub and super, Ladybird matches Firefox
exactly, and Chrome and WebKit to within the 1px above.
